                <pb facs="0898" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg814"/>

                <head>No. 405.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-10-21T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi>
                            21, 1886—11 a.m</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bayard informs Mr. Curry that he is instructed to state to the Government of
                    Spain that the accommodation of all differences is equally and earnestly desired
                    by the President, and that, if notified that the Spanish Government will levy no
                    discrimination against American vessels and cargoes which, they carry from the
                    United States or any foreign country, the proclamation of 1884 will be renewed
                    by him.</p>
            </div>
